 MD.write_text('# Task 12P — V2.2 Postmortem\n\n## Result\n\nV2.2 is a failed research specimen. No redesign or tuning was performed.\n\n## RAF\n\nRAF generalized to several observed cases but regressed protected `neg-03`. The demonstrated cause is actor/action binding: the relation helper accepted sentence-initial `Coordinate` as actor-like and `owner` as displacement evidence, although the sentence describes coordination, not abdication. RAF must be narrowed before any retest.\n\n## TCF\n\nTCF preserved all 34 protected guards and generalized where a required task was tied to a terminal/non-return state. It recovered only `tcf-12` and `tcf-15`; termination-before-delivery, deadline expiry, departure, and `both-07` lack that represented relation. Retain it only for redesign.\n\n## Contextual attachment\n\nProposition scope is rejected. Its 11 guard regressions divide into one helper-isolation breach, eight lost external factual suppressors, and two lost textual-framing suppressors. The evidence supports separate semantic recognition and contextual attachment families, not a universal clause-scope solution.\n\n## Both-07\n\nRAF recovered but the TCF `quit` relation did not. This is `COMPOSITION_DIAGNOSIS_INCOMPLETE`, not evidence for a fourth mechanism.\n\n## Future boundary\n\nAny future experiment requires refined hypotheses, independently frozen evaluation data, explicit protected invariants, true helper isolation, case-level ablation, and no shared-layer semantics.\n')
